#{[17592186351275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351275 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351275 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [1,e].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af621e2e-fd54-5586-bdc4-d3d2f33437c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351275 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{3}{y}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(e-1)[{x}^{4}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({2}^{4}-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =15(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A=3-15(e-1)=18-15e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380859 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186380860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380859 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129940" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380859 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380859 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [e,{e}^{2}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380859 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e6ad635-fec2-5b1b-906a-f0e5dc3a4875" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380859 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{ }(\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{e}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡e) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186380865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380860 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8a844585-2a8a-5020-bb6d-497af9fa7a7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380861 #edb/ref 1080 "2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380861 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380861 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "67efca7f-46bf-526b-bf7c-9f183d920665" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380862 #edb/ref 1080 "e+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380862 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380862 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d1de4ab0-12a4-59ba-8566-42bcdbebcac3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380863 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380863 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17