417] [17592186382407 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1+y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [0,8].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382407 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66d9f9e9-c9db-5bd9-aeae-e3f4c6b82bbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382407 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1+y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}y\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A & =(8-0){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{8}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}y\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{0}^{8}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{8}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1+y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A=3+32=35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186382410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382408 #edb/ref 10